questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot REST API deployed on Tomcat experiences progressive Old Generation memory growth, eventually triggering an `OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` after 48 hours of uptime. A heap dump analysis reveals millions of `TransactionSnapshot` objects surviving in the Old Gen. You trace the issue to the following bean:

java
@Service
public class TransactionAuditor {
    private static final ThreadLocal<List<TransactionSnapshot>> SNAPSHOT_HOLDER = 
            ThreadLocal.withInitial(ArrayList::new);

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
    public void auditTransaction(Transaction txn) {
        List<TransactionSnapshot> list = SNAPSHOT_HOLDER.get();
        list.add(new TransactionSnapshot(txn));
        persistAuditLog(list);
    }

    private void persistAuditLog(List<TransactionSnapshot> list) {
        // Persistence logic writes batch to DB
    }
}
